# Local Supabase connection details, for the VSCode Testing UI.
#
# Why this file exists: the Testing UI runs pytest directly — it does not go through
# scripts/test-local.sh — so nothing exports DATABASE_URL and load_dotenv() falls back
# to backend/.env, which points at the REAL project. Pointing python.envFile here makes
# the Testing UI target the local stack instead. See .vscode/settings.json.
#
# Safe to commit, deliberately not named .env* so the root .gitignore does not swallow
# it. These are the Supabase CLI's fixed local development credentials — identical on
# every machine, publicly documented, and only ever valid against 127.0.0.1. They are
# NOT secrets. Real credentials live in backend/.env, which IS gitignored.
#
# Requires `supabase start`. Without it these tests fail with connection refused,
# which is the correct and obvious failure.

